      "result_description": "Letchworth Garden City CC - 1st XI - Won",
      "result_applied_to": "219",
      "match_notes": "<p>A&nbsp;storming&nbsp;win&nbsp;for&nbsp;Letchworth&nbsp;to&nbsp;kick&nbsp;off&nbsp;the&nbsp;league&nbsp;season.&nbsp;The&nbsp;groundstaff&nbsp;team&nbsp;worked&nbsp;wonders&nbsp;to&nbsp;get&nbsp;the&nbsp;game&nbsp;off&nbsp;on&nbsp;time&nbsp;and&nbsp;despite&nbsp;being&nbsp;stuck&nbsp;in&nbsp;on&nbsp;a&nbsp;lively&nbsp;looking&nbsp;deck&nbsp;Letchworth&nbsp;started&nbsp;well&nbsp;Aitkenhead&nbsp;and&nbsp;Sprittles&nbsp;added&nbsp;75&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;first&nbsp;wicket.&nbsp;That&nbsp;quickly&nbsp;became&nbsp;82/3&nbsp;but&nbsp;Kendle&nbsp;and&nbsp;Albon&nbsp;steadied&nbsp;the&nbsp;ship.&nbsp;Albon&nbsp;went&nbsp;for&nbsp;50&nbsp;and&nbsp;Letchworth&nbsp;closed&nbsp;194/8&nbsp;which&nbsp;looked&nbsp;above&nbsp;par.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>So&nbsp;it&nbsp;proved&nbsp;as&nbsp;Sprittles&nbsp;and&nbsp;Aussie&nbsp;Josh&nbsp;restricted&nbsp;Ampthill&nbsp;to&nbsp;22/1&nbsp;from&nbsp;the&nbsp;first&nbsp;15&nbsp;overs.&nbsp;It&nbsp;was&nbsp;all&nbsp;Letchworth&nbsp;from&nbsp;there&nbsp;on&nbsp;with&nbsp;Liam&nbsp;Bishton&nbsp;picking&nbsp;up&nbsp;an&nbsp;excellent&nbsp;3/16&nbsp;as&nbsp;Ampthill&nbsp;slowly&nbsp;trudged&nbsp;to&nbsp;126/9.</p>\r\n",
